new file mode 100644
index 0000000..83014c7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/timers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Question timer
+
+## Moderator workflow
+
+New quiz and **Quiz settings** both have numeric **Timer minutes** and
+**Timer seconds** fields. Both default to 0; together, 0 means no timer.
+They accept nonnegative whole numbers. Seconds above 59 are accepted and
+normalized into minutes on the next settings load. The combined duration is
+bounded at 4,294,967,295 seconds to keep deadline arithmetic safe. Invalid
+submissions retain the entered fields and never partially update the quiz.
+
+The duration applies to every active question of a **new live game**. As with
+questions and prize settings, creating a game snapshots its timer setting:
+changing the source quiz does not unexpectedly change a game already running.
+Client-only previews remain untimed.
+
+The big screen displays a large `M:SS` countdown only while a timed question
+is open. Players never receive timer fields or a timer element. At expiration,
+the question closes and shows the exact same results/controls as **Finish**;
+it does not automatically advance to the next question. **Finish** remains
+available to close a question early. **Next** starts a fresh duration.
+
+## Authority and persistence
+
+- `quizzes.timer_seconds` and `games.timer_seconds` store total seconds. Additive,
+  idempotent migrations default existing quizzes and games to no timer.
+- `games.opened_at` is an existing persisted UTC timestamp in microseconds.
+  Only Start/Next opening a question writes it. Deadline = opened_at + duration.
+  Reading state, reloading, polling, and process restarts never move the deadline.
+- A server worker checks every 100 ms, even without connected browsers. An
+  atomic SQL update changes expired open questions to `closed` and increments
+  their version once. It broadcasts through both existing watch channels so
+  moderator screens and phones immediately receive normal closed state.
+- Startup expires overdue games before opening the HTTP listener. Every game
+  request also checks expiration under the same database mutex used for answer
+  and moderator writes. Thus answers arriving after the deadline cannot exploit
+  the gap between worker ticks. A stale Finish racing with expiration gets the
+  existing conflict response; it cannot advance or close a second question.
+- Only moderator open-state payloads include `deadline_at` and `server_now`
+  (milliseconds). The display uses their difference and a monotonic browser
+  clock (`performance.now()`), not the browser's wall clock. Display updates do
+  not submit Finish requests or broadcast timer ticks to players. The server is
+  authoritative even if a browser is offline or its JavaScript is suspended.
+- Timer configuration is intentionally absent from `QuizContents` and exported
+  JSON. Imports start with the default no-timer setting, even if supplied JSON
+  contains unknown timer keys. The portable export schema is unchanged.
+
+## Tests (all offline)
+
+```sh
+cargo test --offline --locked
+cargo clippy --offline --locked -- -D warnings
+cargo build --release --offline --locked
+python3 tests/timer.py
+# With bin/serve running, using the standard test credentials or test env vars:
+python3 tests/timer_browser.py
+```
+
+Rust tests cover exact microsecond boundaries, idempotent expiration/migrations,
+zero duration, validation and arithmetic overflow, snapshot isolation, export
+exclusion and import defaults, and player payload privacy. `timer.py` starts its
+own isolated server/database under `storage/`; it checks settings/errors,
+long-poll wakeup, correct results, late-answer rejection, no-browser expiration,
+early Finish, Next deadlines, and abrupt restarts before/after expiration.
+`timer_browser.py` drives installed Chromium via the stdlib-only CDP helper to
+verify exact labels, numeric fields, persistence, minute/second formatting,
+reload continuity, timer absence on phones, automatic results, and zero timers.
diff --git a/src/game.rs b/src/game.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2cfb13e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/game.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,784 @@
+use crate::{
+    App, html,
+    model::{self, Draft, Form, Quiz},
+    not_found, views,
+};
+use axum::{
+    body::to_bytes,
+    extract::Request,
+    http::{StatusCode, header},
+    response::{IntoResponse, Redirect, Response},
+};
+use rusqlite::{Connection, OptionalExtension, params};
+use serde_json::{Value, json};
+use std::time::Duration;
+
+pub fn initialize(db: &Connection) -> rusqlite::Result<()> {
+    db.execute_batch("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS games (
+        code TEXT PRIMARY KEY, quiz_id INTEGER NOT NULL, title TEXT NOT NULL,
+        questions TEXT NOT NULL, phase TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'waiting', position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
+        version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0);
+        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS players (
+        game TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES games(code), token TEXT NOT NULL, name TEXT NOT NULL,
+        seen INTEGER NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(game,token));
+        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS answers (
+        game TEXT NOT NULL, player TEXT NOT NULL, question INTEGER NOT NULL, choice INTEGER NOT NULL,
+        PRIMARY KEY(game,player,question), FOREIGN KEY(game,player) REFERENCES players(game,token));
+        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS winners (
+            game TEXT NOT NULL, player TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(game,player),
+            FOREIGN KEY(game,player) REFERENCES players(game,token));")?;
+    model::add_column(
+        db,
+        "games",
+        "number_of_winners",
+        "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 3 CHECK(number_of_winners >= 1)",
+    )?;
+    model::add_column(
+        db,
+        "games",
+        "timer_seconds",
+        "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK(timer_seconds BETWEEN 0 AND 4294967295)",
+    )?;
+    model::add_column(db, "games", "opened_at", "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0")?;
+    db.execute_batch("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS games_timers ON games(opened_at) WHERE phase='open' AND timer_seconds>0;")?;
+    model::add_column(db, "answers", "elapsed", "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0")
+}
+fn random(db: &Connection, bytes: i64) -> rusqlite::Result<String> {
+    db.query_row("SELECT lower(hex(randomblob(?)))", [bytes], |r| r.get(0))
+}
+pub fn create(db: &mut Connection, quiz: &Quiz) -> rusqlite::Result<Response> {
+    let questions: Vec<_> = model::QuizContents::from_quiz(quiz, model::questions(db, quiz.id)?)
+        .questions
+        .into_iter()
+        .filter(|q| q.active)
+        .collect();
+    let code = random(db, 5)?.to_uppercase();
+    db.execute(
+        "INSERT INTO games(code,quiz_id,title,questions,number_of_winners,timer_seconds) VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?)",
+        params![
+            code,
+            quiz.id,
+            quiz.title,
+            serde_json::to_string(&questions).unwrap(),
+            quiz.number_of_winners,
+            quiz.timer_seconds
+        ],
+    )?;
+    Ok(Redirect::to(&format!("/moderate/games/{code}")).into_response())
+}
+struct Game {
+    title: String,
+    questions: Vec<Draft>,
+    phase: String,
+    position: usize,
+    version: i64,
+    number_of_winners: i64,
+    opened_at: i64,
+    timer_seconds: i64,
+}
+fn load(db: &Connection, code: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<Option<Game>> {
+    db.query_row(
+        "SELECT title,questions,phase,position,version,number_of_winners,opened_at,timer_seconds FROM games WHERE code=?",
+        [code],
+        |r| {
+            let raw: String = r.get(1)?;
+            Ok(Game {
+                title: r.get(0)?,
+                questions: serde_json::from_str(&raw).expect("saved questions"),
+                phase: r.get(2)?,
+                position: r.get(3)?,
+                version: r.get(4)?,
+                number_of_winners: r.get(5)?,
+                opened_at: r.get(6)?,
+                timer_seconds: r.get(7)?,
+            })
+        },
+    )
+    .optional()
+}
+/// Server timestamps in microseconds; persisted so a restart preserves answer timing.
+fn now_micros() -> i64 {
+    std::time::SystemTime::now()
+        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)
+        .expect("system clock")
+        .as_micros() as i64
+}
+
+/// The same closed phase/version transition as Finish, serialized with all writes.
+/// Taking `now` explicitly also allows deterministic boundary tests.
+fn expire_due(db: &Connection, now: i64) -> rusqlite::Result<usize> {
+    db.execute(
+        "UPDATE games SET phase='closed',version=version+1
+         WHERE phase='open' AND timer_seconds>0 AND opened_at<=? - timer_seconds*1000000",
+        [now],
+    )
+}
+pub fn expire(app: &App, db: &Connection) -> rusqlite::Result<()> {
+    if expire_due(db, now_micros())? > 0 {
+        app.changes.send_modify(|v| *v += 1);
+        app.phases.send_replace(*app.changes.borrow());
+    }
+    Ok(())
+}
+
+/// No browser or active long poll is required for expiration. Also run on startup
+/// and before each game request so late answers cannot slip between worker ticks.
+pub fn start_timer_worker(app: App) {
+    tokio::spawn(async move {
+        let mut tick = tokio::time::interval(Duration::from_millis(100));
+        tick.set_missed_tick_behavior(tokio::time::MissedTickBehavior::Skip);
+        loop {
+            tick.tick().await;
+            let app = app.clone();
+            let result = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {
+                let db = app.db.lock().expect("database lock");
+                expire(&app, &db)
+            })
+            .await;
+            if !matches!(result, Ok(Ok(()))) {
+                eprintln!("Timer expiration failed: {result:?}");
+            }
+        }
+    });
+}
+
+#[derive(Debug, serde::Serialize)]
+struct Standing {
+    #[serde(skip)]
+    token: String,
+    name: String,
+    points: usize,
+    #[serde(skip)]
+    elapsed: i64,
+    place: usize,
+    winner: bool,
+}
+
+fn leaderboard(db: &Connection, code: &str, g: &Game) -> rusqlite::Result<Vec<Standing>> {
+    let mut rows = db.prepare("SELECT token,name,EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM winners w WHERE w.game=p.game AND w.player=p.token) FROM players p WHERE game=? ORDER BY rowid")?
+        .query_map([code], |r| Ok(Standing { token: r.get(0)?, name: r.get(1)?, winner: r.get(2)?, points: 0, elapsed: 0, place: 0 }))?
+        .collect::<rusqlite::Result<Vec<_>>>()?;
+    let indices: std::collections::HashMap<_, _> = rows
+        .iter()
+        .enumerate()
+        .map(|(i, p)| (p.token.clone(), i))
+        .collect();
+    let mut answers =
+        db.prepare("SELECT player,question,choice,elapsed FROM answers WHERE game=?")?;
+    let mut answers = answers.query([code])?;
+    while let Some(answer) = answers.next()? {
+        let question: usize = answer.get(1)?;
+        let choice: usize = answer.get(2)?;
+        if g.questions
+            .get(question)
+            .and_then(|q| q.options.get(choice))
+            .is_some_and(|o| o.correct)
+        {
+            let token: String = answer.get(0)?;
+            if let Some(&i) = indices.get(&token) {
+                rows[i].points += 1;
+                rows[i].elapsed += answer.get::<_, i64>(3)?;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    // Stable sort: exact point/time ties retain join order, including zero-point players.
+    rows.sort_by_key(|r| (std::cmp::Reverse(r.points), r.elapsed));
+    for (i, row) in rows.iter_mut().enumerate() {
+        row.place = i + 1;
+    }
+    Ok(rows)
+}
+
+/// Called inside the same transaction as the game revision update.
+fn select_winners(db: &Connection, code: &str, g: &Game, command: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<()> {
+    let eligible: Vec<_> = leaderboard(db, code, g)?
+        .into_iter()
+        .filter(|r| r.points > 0)
+        .collect();
+    let n = (g.number_of_winners as usize).min(eligible.len());
+    let mut selected = Vec::new();
+    if command == "top" {
+        selected.extend(eligible.iter().take(n).map(|r| r.token.clone()));
+    } else if command == "draw" && n > 0 {
+        let cutoff = eligible[n - 1].points;
+        selected.extend(
+            eligible
+                .iter()
+                .filter(|r| r.points > cutoff)
+                .map(|r| r.token.clone()),
+        );
+        let tied: std::collections::HashSet<_> = eligible
+            .iter()
+            .filter(|r| r.points == cutoff)
+            .map(|r| r.token.as_str())
+            .collect();
+        // SQLite supplies a fresh random permutation on every draw. Speed is not used.
+        let random_order = db
+            .prepare("SELECT token FROM players WHERE game=? ORDER BY random()")?
+            .query_map([code], |r| r.get::<_, String>(0))?
+            .collect::<rusqlite::Result<Vec<_>>>()?;
+        let remaining = n - selected.len();
+        selected.extend(
+            random_order
+                .into_iter()
+                .filter(|t| tied.contains(t.as_str()))
+                .take(remaining),
+        );
+    }
+    db.execute("DELETE FROM winners WHERE game=?", [code])?;
+    for token in selected {
+        db.execute(
+            "INSERT INTO winners(game,player) VALUES (?,?)",
+            params![code, token],
+        )?;
+    }
+    Ok(())
+}
+
+fn player(db: &Connection, code: &str, token: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<Option<String>> {
+    db.query_row(
+        "SELECT name FROM players WHERE game=? AND token=?",
+        params![code, token],
+        |r| r.get(0),
+    )
+    .optional()
+}
+fn touch(db: &Connection, code: &str, token: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<bool> {
+    let returning: bool = db.query_row(
+        "SELECT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM players WHERE game=? AND token=? AND seen < unixepoch()-35)",
+        params![code, token],
+        |r| r.get(0),
+    )?;
+    db.execute(
+        "UPDATE players SET seen=unixepoch() WHERE game=? AND token=?",
+        params![code, token],
+    )?;
+    Ok(returning)
+}
+fn state(
+    db: &Connection,
+    code: &str,
+    token: &str,
+    moderator: bool,
+    g: &Game,
+    revision: u64,
+) -> rusqlite::Result<Value> {
+    let name = player(db, code, token)?;
+    let mut s = json!({"title":g.title,"phase":g.phase,"version":g.version,"revision":revision,"name":name,"total":g.questions.len()});
+    if moderator {
+        if g.phase == "open" && g.timer_seconds > 0 {
+            s["deadline_at"] = ((g.opened_at + g.timer_seconds * 1_000_000) / 1000).into();
+            s["server_now"] = (now_micros() / 1000).into();
+        }
+        s["players"] = db
+            .query_row(
+                "SELECT count(*) FROM players WHERE game=? AND seen>=unixepoch()-35",
+                [code],
+                |r| r.get::<_, i64>(0),
+            )?
+            .into();
+    }
+    if g.phase == "ended" {
+        let rows = leaderboard(db, code, g)?;
+        if moderator {
+            s["number_of_winners"] = g.number_of_winners.into();
+            s["leaderboard"] = json!(rows);
+        } else if let Some(row) = rows.iter().find(|r| r.token == token) {
+            s["place"] = row.place.into();
+            s["player_count"] = rows.len().into();
+            s["points"] = row.points.into();
+            s["winner"] = row.winner.into();
+        }
+    }
+    if g.phase == "open" || g.phase == "closed" {
+        // Unjoined browsers receive no question data. Correctness is never serialized while open.
+        if !moderator && name.is_none() {
+            return Ok(s);
+        }
+        let q = &g.questions[g.position];
+        let pick: Option<usize> = db
+            .query_row(
+                "SELECT choice FROM answers WHERE game=? AND player=? AND question=?",
+                params![code, token, g.position],
+                |r| r.get(0),
+            )
+            .optional()?;
+        s["position"] = g.position.into();
+        s["question"] = q.text.clone().into();
+        s["pick"] = json!(pick);
+        let mut options = Vec::new();
+        for (i, o) in q.options.iter().enumerate() {
+            let mut option = json!({"text":o.text});
+            if g.phase == "closed" {
+                option["correct"] = o.correct.into();
+                if moderator {
+                    option["count"] = db
+                        .query_row(
+                            "SELECT count(*) FROM answers WHERE game=? AND question=? AND choice=?",
+                            params![code, g.position, i],
+                            |r| r.get::<_, i64>(0),
+                        )?
+                        .into();
+                }
+            }
+            options.push(option);
+        }
+        s["options"] = options.into();
+        if moderator {
+            s["answers"] = db.query_row("SELECT count(*) FROM answers a JOIN players p ON p.game=a.game AND p.token=a.player WHERE a.game=? AND a.question=? AND p.seen>=unixepoch()-35", params![code,g.position], |r| r.get::<_,i64>(0))?.into();
+        } else if g.phase == "closed" {
+            s["result"] = match pick {
+                None => "No answer",
+                Some(i) if q.options[i].correct => "Correct!",
+                _ => "Wrong!",
+            }
+            .into();
+        }
+    }
+    Ok(s)
+}
+fn shell(code: &str, g: &Game, moderator: bool, token: &str, join: &str) -> String {
+    let e = views::escape;
+    let body = format!(
+        r#"<main class="live-main {}" id="live" data-moderator="{moderator}" data-base="{}" data-token="{}"><div class="live-heading"><span class="eyebrow">{} · LIVE QUIZ</span><h1>{}</h1></div><section id="live-content" aria-live="polite">Connecting…</section><section id="join-info" {}><p>Join the quiz on your phone</p><a class="join-link" href="{}">{}</a><img class="join-qr" src="/moderate/games/{code}/qr.svg" alt="QR code for the join link" width="240" height="240"></section><p id="live-status" role="status"></p><noscript>Enable JavaScript to join and follow the live quiz.</noscript></main><script src="/assets/live.js" defer></script>"#,
+        if moderator { "big-screen" } else { "phone" },
+        if moderator {
+            format!("/moderate/games/{code}")
+        } else {
+            format!("/play/{code}")
+        },
+        e(token),
+        if moderator { "BIG SCREEN" } else { "QUIZZY" },
+        e(&g.title),
+        if moderator && g.phase == "waiting" {
+            ""
+        } else {
+            "hidden"
+        },
+        e(join),
+        e(join)
+    );
+    // Public pages contain neither moderator tokens nor moderator navigation.
+    if moderator {
+        views::page(&g.title, &body, token)
+    } else {
+        format!(r#"<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{} · Quizzy</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/quizzy.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app.css"></head><body>{}</body></html>"#,e(&g.title),body.replace(&format!("<img class=\"join-qr\" src=\"/moderate/games/{code}/qr.svg\" alt=\"QR code for the join link\" width=\"240\" height=\"240\">"), ""))
+    }
+}
+
+pub async fn handle(app: App, req: Request, moderator: bool) -> Response {
+    let path = req.uri().path().trim_end_matches('/').to_owned();
+    let parts: Vec<_> = path.split('/').collect();
+    let offset = if moderator { 3 } else { 2 };
+    if parts.len() < offset + 1 || parts.len() > offset + 2 {
+        return not_found();
+    }
+    let code = parts[offset].to_owned();
+    let action = parts.get(offset + 1).copied().unwrap_or("").to_owned();
+    let method = req.method().as_str().to_owned();
+    if !["GET", "POST", "HEAD"].contains(&method.as_str()) {
+        return StatusCode::METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED.into_response();
+    }
+    let query: Form =
+        serde_urlencoded::from_str(req.uri().query().unwrap_or("")).unwrap_or_default();
+    let since = query.get("since").and_then(|x| x.parse::<u64>().ok());
+    let host = req
+        .headers()
+        .get(header::HOST)
+        .and_then(|h| h.to_str().ok())
+        .unwrap_or("localhost:3000")
+        .to_owned();
+    let cookie = req
+        .headers()
+        .get(header::COOKIE)
+        .and_then(|h| h.to_str().ok())
+        .unwrap_or("")
+        .split(';')
+        .find_map(|part| part.trim().strip_prefix("quizzy_player="))
+        .filter(|v| v.len() == 64 && v.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit()))
+        .unwrap_or("")
+        .to_owned();
+    let form: Form = if method == "POST" {
+        let Ok(bytes) = to_bytes(req.into_body(), 8192).await else {
+            return StatusCode::PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE.into_response();
+        };
+        let Ok(form) = serde_urlencoded::from_bytes(&bytes) else {
+            return StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST.into_response();
+        };
+        form
+    } else {
+        Form::new()
+    };
+    if method == "POST"
+        && !form
+            .get("csrf")
+            .is_some_and(|t| !t.is_empty() && t == if moderator { &app.csrf } else { &cookie })
+    {
+        return (
+            StatusCode::FORBIDDEN,
+            "Invalid form token. Reload and try again.",
+        )
+            .into_response();
+    }
+    let mut changes = if moderator {
+        app.changes.subscribe()
+    } else {
+        app.phases.subscribe()
+    };
+    if action == "state" && method == "GET" && since == Some(*changes.borrow_and_update()) {
+        let _ = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(10), changes.changed()).await;
+    }
+    let result = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || -> rusqlite::Result<Response> {
+        let db = app.db.lock().expect("database lock");
+        expire(&app, &db)?;
+        let Some(mut g) = load(&db,&code)? else { return Ok(not_found()); };
+        let token = if cookie.is_empty() {random(&db,32)?} else {cookie.clone()};
+        let csrf = if moderator {app.csrf.as_str()} else {token.as_str()};
+        let join = format!("http://{host}/play/{code}");
+        if method == "GET" || method == "HEAD" {
+            if action.is_empty() {
+                let mut response = html(shell(&code,&g,moderator,csrf,&join));
+                if !moderator && cookie.is_empty() {
+                    response.headers_mut().insert(header::SET_COOKIE, format!("quizzy_player={token}; Path=/play; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Max-Age=31536000").parse().unwrap());
+                }
+                return Ok(response);
+            }
+            if action == "qr.svg" && moderator {
+                let Ok(qr) = qrcode::QrCode::new(join.as_bytes()) else {
+                    return Ok((StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST, "Host name is too long for a QR code").into_response());
+                };
+                let w = qr.width();
+                let mut svg = format!(r#"<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 {} {}"><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="white"/><path fill="black" d=""#,w+8,w+8);
+                for y in 0..w { for x in 0..w { if qr[(x,y)] == qrcode::Color::Dark { svg.push_str(&format!("M{} {}h1v1h-1z",x+4,y+4)); } } }
+                svg.push_str("\"/></svg>");
+                return Ok(([(header::CONTENT_TYPE,"image/svg+xml")],svg).into_response());
+            }
+            if action != "state" { return Ok(not_found()); }
+            if !moderator && g.phase != "ended" && touch(&db,&code,&token)? { app.changes.send_modify(|v| *v+=1); }
+        } else {
+            match (moderator,action.as_str()) {
+                (false,"join") => {
+                    if g.phase == "ended" { return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"The quiz is over").into_response()); }
+                    let name = form.get("name").map(|s| s.trim()).unwrap_or("");
+                    if name.is_empty() || name.chars().count()>80 { return Ok((StatusCode::UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,"Enter your name (1–80 characters).").into_response()); }
+                    db.execute("INSERT INTO players(game,token,name,seen) VALUES (?,?,?,unixepoch()) ON CONFLICT(game,token) DO UPDATE SET seen=unixepoch()",params![code,token,name])?;
+                }
+                (false,"answer") => {
+                    let position = form.get("position").and_then(|s| s.parse::<usize>().ok());
+                    let choice = form.get("choice").and_then(|s| s.parse::<usize>().ok());
+                    if g.phase != "open" || position != Some(g.position) || choice.is_none_or(|c| c >= g.questions[g.position].options.len()) || player(&db,&code,&token)?.is_none() {
+                        return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"This question is no longer open. Reconnecting…").into_response());
+                    }
+                    db.execute("INSERT INTO answers(game,player,question,choice,elapsed) VALUES (?,?,?,?,?) ON CONFLICT(game,player,question) DO UPDATE SET choice=excluded.choice,elapsed=excluded.elapsed",params![code,token,g.position,choice.unwrap(),now_micros().saturating_sub(g.opened_at).max(0)])?;
+                    touch(&db,&code,&token)?;
+                }
+                (true,"action") => {
+                    if form.get("version").and_then(|s| s.parse::<i64>().ok()) != Some(g.version) { return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"The game has already moved on.").into_response()); }
+                    let command = form.get("command").map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("");
+                    let tx = db.unchecked_transaction()?;
+                    match (g.phase.as_str(),command) {
+                        ("waiting","start") => g.phase = if g.questions.is_empty() {"ended"} else {"open"}.into(),
+                        ("open","finish") => g.phase="closed".into(),
+                        ("closed","next") if g.position+1<g.questions.len() => {g.position+=1; g.phase="open".into();},
+                        ("closed","end") if g.position+1==g.questions.len() => g.phase="ended".into(),
+                        ("ended", "top" | "draw" | "reset") => select_winners(&tx, &code, &g, command)?,
+                        _ => return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"Invalid game transition").into_response())
+                    }
+                    g.version+=1;
+                    if g.phase == "open" { g.opened_at = now_micros(); }
+                    tx.execute("UPDATE games SET phase=?,position=?,version=?,opened_at=? WHERE code=?",params![g.phase,g.position,g.version,g.opened_at,code])?;
+                    tx.commit()?;
+                }
+                _ => return Ok(not_found())
+            }
+            app.changes.send_modify(|v| *v+=1);
+            if moderator { app.phases.send_replace(*app.changes.borrow()); }
+        }
+        let mut state = state(&db,&code,&token,moderator,&g,*app.changes.borrow())?;
+        state["cursor"] = if moderator { *app.changes.borrow() } else { *app.phases.borrow() }.into();
+        Ok(axum::Json(state).into_response())
+    }).await;
+    match result {
+        Ok(Ok(response)) => response,
+        error => {
+            eprintln!("Game request failed: {error:?}");
+            (
+                StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,
+                "Unable to load game. Please try again.",
+            )
+                .into_response()
+        }
+    }
+}
